state/

# ...EXCEPT the curated DNA seed memories every mother inherits at birth. The
# special bake tars this tree onto a fresh mother, so these must be committed —
# otherwise a clean checkout (or any machine without Pete's working-tree copies)
# births a memory-less mother that re-learns "births go through the cells CLI"
# the hard way. git can't re-include files under an ignored dir without
# re-including each parent level first, hence the staircase. The global mother's
# LIVE accumulators (roster + activity log) stay ignored — they're per-mother
# churn, rebuilt from her own births, never seeded into a project mother.
!dna/specials/mother/state/
dna/specials/mother/state/*
!dna/specials/mother/state/memory/
dna/specials/mother/state/memory/*
!dna/specials/mother/state/memory/MEMORY.md
!dna/specials/mother/state/memory/feedback_use_cells_cli.md
!dna/specials/mother/state/memory/feedback_explain_jargon.md
!dna/specials/mother/state/memory/feedback_memory_freshness.md
!dna/specials/mother/state/memory/reference_pi_internals.md
!dna/specials/mother/state/memory/reference_sprite_hibernation.md
!dna/specials/mother/state/memory/project_mother_proxy.md

.env
.env.local
.envrc
*.log
.DS_Store
node_modules/
dist/
build/
# Python bytecode (e.g. hermes model-provider plugin compile artifacts)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pi/.cache/
.pi/npm/
# only the top-level memory dir (cell-keeper's data) — NOT the memory extension code under template/.pi/
/memory/

# Internal working docs — kept out of public-release tree.
JOURNAL.md
BOARD.md
BOARD.html
PLAN.md
PLAN.html
STATUS.md
STATUS.html
NEEDS_PETE.md

# Private .claude/ infra — keep .claude/skills/ tracked but exclude the rest.
.claude/.steward-silent-until
.claude/.pete-loop.active
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/commands/
.claude/hooks/
.claude/loops/
.claude/sent-pings/
.claude/worktrees/

# Gemini Antigravity CLI config symlink (per-machine)
.antigravitycli/
